## Web Real-Time Communication Techniques

## Comparison Table

| Technique | Direction | Protocol | Latency | Complexity | Use Case |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Short Polling | Client→Server | HTTP | High (interval-bound) | Low | Simple dashboards |
| Long Polling | Client→Server (held) | HTTP | Medium | Medium | Notifications |
| SSE / EventSource | Server→Client only | HTTP | Low | Low | Live feeds, AI streaming |
| WebSocket | Full-duplex | WS | Very low | Medium | Chat, gaming, collab |
| WebRTC | Peer-to-peer | UDP/DTLS | Ultra-low | High | Video calls, P2P |

## Decision Flow

```
Need real-time?
  Yes
    ├── Server push only (no client messages)?
    │     └── Use SSE/EventSource (simpler, HTTP-compatible)
    ├── Full bidirectional?
    │     └── Use WebSocket
    └── Audio/video or P2P?
          └── Use WebRTC
  No → Use HTTP REST
```

## Quick Reference

```javascript
// Short Polling
setInterval(() => fetch('/api/data').then(update), 3000);

// Long Polling
async function poll() {
  const r = await fetch('/api/wait');
  handle(await r.json()); poll();
}

// SSE
const es = new EventSource('/api/stream');
es.onmessage = e => handle(e.data);

// WebSocket
const ws = new WebSocket('wss://example.com');
ws.onmessage = e => handle(e.data);
ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'ping' }));
```

